         ("Why do hesitant local shop owners often swing behind permanent pedestrian improvements after pilot trials?", ["Hard ninety-day data frequently demonstrates calmer speeds alongside higher walking foot traffic.", "Municipal drivers hand free restaurant meal coupons cleanly out of buses.", "Heavy barricades lock private customer vehicles outside town perimeters forever.", "Planter boxes double neighborhood property tax bills promptly."], 0, "ITP-MOD-05", "B2", "Data empiris 90 hari sering membuktikan meningkatnya pengunjung pejalan kaki di depan toko."),
         ("The word 'nimble' in sentence 2 is closest in meaning to:", ["agile", "stubborn", "costly", "ancient"], 0, "ITP-MOD-05", "B2", "'A nimble movement' bermakna gerakan yang gesit/fleksibel."),
         ("What core advantage does reversibility give engineers during temporary plaza testing?", ["Flawed lane widths or bus turns can be spotted and tweaked cleanly before permanent concrete pouring.", "Traffic lights stop consuming winter electrical current entirely.", "Neighborhood children keep all wooden street flowerpots permanently afterward.", "Sidewalk contractors bypass safety vests during sunny Saturday shifts."], 0, "ITP-MOD-05", "B2", "Sifat dapat diubah memungkinkan revisi cepat sebelum konstruksi permanen yang mahal dibangun."),
         ("The phrase 'turn sluggish timelines upside down' means:", ["radically accelerating initial real-world implementation", "posting calendar posters upside down atop city halls", "canceling street engineering exams for incoming university interns", "pouring wet concrete straight into frozen January ditches"], 0, "ITP-MOD-10", "B2", "Frasa idiomatis bermakna membalik pola lamban menjadi implementasi uji cepat."),
